sponseId":"msg_011Ce77i7VBysbzFUB33jn8w","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01FY2nbMneNPLZBLyotjPwgJ","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"NAME\",\"SUMLEV\",\"POPESTIMATE2025\"\n\"United States\",10,341784857\n\"California\",40,39355309\n\"New York\",40,20002427\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914752724},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see:\n- SUMLEV=10 is the U.S. total\n- SUMLEV=40 is state-level data\n- NAME='United States' shows the total U.S. population of 341,784,857 for 2025\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Get the total farmers markets from the farmers_markets table\n2. Use the census data with NAME='United States' for the total population\n3. Create a build script that joins these two to calculate the ratio\n\nActually, wait. Let me think about this more carefully. The farmers_markets table is already by state, so I need to:\n1. Sum all farmers_markets in the farmers_markets table (total across all states)\n2. Get the U.S. population from the census data (NAME='United States')\n3. Calculate the ratio\n\nLet me create a build script that does this.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01VF52Qavi48wVW2UcY2sB58","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener(); _o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]; u.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\nmarkets = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"markets\", storage_options=so)\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"census\", storage_options=so)\n\n# Sum all farmers markets across states\ntotals_markets = markets.aggregate(total_farmers_markets=markets.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US population from census (NAME='United States')\nus_pop = (census.filter(census.NAME == 'United States')\n          .select('POPESTIMATE2025').mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join and calculate ratio\nexpr = (\n    totals_markets.join(us_pop, totals_markets.k == us_pop.k)\n      .mutate(markets_per_100k=totals_markets.total_farmers_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select('total_farmers_markets', 'POPESTIMATE2025', 'markets_per_100k')\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":743,"cacheRead":18425,"cacheWrite":261,"totalTokens":19441,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.0037150000000000004,"cacheRead":0.0018425000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.00032625,"total":0.005895750000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":205},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914752735,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77iQ371XjkEoayz6qBW","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01VF52Qavi48wVW2UcY2sB58","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1244 bytes to .xorq/scripts/build_markets_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914760931},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I'll build and add this to the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_0127vWUuNFzeNbvFRmEkRuxE","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/trial-pi-35-5g3dwt8p && xorq build .xorq/scripts/build_markets_per_capita.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/bp3.txt && cat /tmp/bp3.txt"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":144,"cacheRead":18686,"cacheWrite":785,"totalTokens":19628,"cost":{"input":0.0